# Orchestration — Plan, Delegate, Ship

Extends `~/.cursor/rules/leo-system-wide.mdc` § Sub-Agent Delegation. Project-specific routing below.

## Planning is delegation-first

When producing an implementation plan (Plan mode, issue spec, or ad-hoc scope), **do not implement in the same step**. The plan MUST include:

1. **Sub-agent map** — one row per work chunk: `Chunk | Owner (sub-agent) | Deliverable | Depends on`
2. **Owner = a named sub-agent** from `~/.cursor/agents/` or the built-in `Explore` / `Plan` agents — not "main agent" or "me"
3. **Right-sized delegation** — match scope to agent count (see table)
4. **Verification plan** — ends with live-server E2E when UI/API changes; dev-env smoke when shipping via `ship-feature` skill
5. **Explicit sign-off** — unresolved decisions listed before execution

Solo plans where the orchestrator implements every chunk are **not acceptable**. Exception: trivial single-file edits (typo, dep bump, one-line config).

| Scope | Delegation |
| --- | --- |
| 1 file, < 50 lines | 1 specialist sub-agent |
| 2–5 files, one layer | 1–2 sub-agents |
| Backend + frontend + tests | Specialist per layer; parallel when independent |
| New subsystem, 5+ files | data, services, routers, frontend, qa separately |

## Sub-agent routing (health-tracker)

| Touch area | Sub-agent |
| --- | --- |
| `apps/marrow/backend/app/**`, migrations, API tests | `fastapi-backend` |
| `apps/marrow/frontend/**` | `frontend-dev` |
| `libs/backend/**` | `fastapi-backend` |
| `libs/ui/**` | `frontend-dev` |
| Workspaces, Nx, CI, Fly deploy | `devops` |
| `apps/marrow/backend/scripts/**`, `apps/marrow/backend/data/**`, ETL | `data-engineer` |
| ML prompts, classification, vision analysis | `data-scientist` |
| Docker, `.github/`, Fly deploy | `devops` |
| QA gate, test matrix, e2e evidence | `qa-engineer` |
| Read-only codebase recon | `Explore` |
| Architecture / plan-only pass | `Plan` |

**Model policy:** every sub-agent runs on `composer-2.5` only.

## Sub-agent brief (every dispatch)

Each brief MUST include:

1. Read `~/.cursor/agent-memory/<agent-name>/MEMORY.md` first
2. Read project `AGENTS.md` and relevant `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`
3. House rules: think / simplify / surgical / goal-driven (Karpathy four)
4. Scope: plan slice with file paths and acceptance criteria
5. Write back gotchas to memory when done

Template: `.cursor/skills/ship-feature/references/sub-agent-brief-template.md`

## End-to-end shipping

For idea or GitHub issue implementation through develop → dev smoke → main PR, use the **`ship-feature`** skill (`.cursor/skills/ship-feature/SKILL.md`).
